{
  "name": "Planning Your Garage Conversion: Where to Start?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you're ready to convert your garage into a more usable space? That's exciting! Getting started with a clear plan is key to a smooth process. First things first, define the new use of the space. Will it be a home office, an extra bedroom, a play area, or something else entirely? This initial decision will dictate all subsequent steps. Once you know its purpose, evaluate the existing structure and consider any utility needs. Will you need new electrical outlets, plumbing for a bathroom, or improved insulation for comfort? These are big questions that impact the scope. Next, it's smart to obtain multiple detailed bids from experienced contractors. Don't just look at the bottom line; compare their proposed process, materials, and timelines. Finally, confirm how your chosen contractor, like HH Remodeling LLC, will handle each stage—from design and demolition to installation and inspections. This includes navigating local building and zoning offices for permits, which are almost always needed for structural changes or significant electrical/plumbing work. We're here to guide homeowners through these steps in communities like Aurora, Westminster, and Boulder.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
